# NO line-ending conversion, anywhere, ever.
#
# Three releases in a row shipped a tree-hash pin that no clean clone could
# reproduce: the pin was computed over CRLF bytes on the authoring machine,
# git converted them to LF at commit, and a Windows clone with autocrlf
# produced a third value. 57 of 57 files failed their own SHA256SUMS on a
# fresh clone. A hash pin is a promise about BYTES; git must not rewrite them.
* -text
